course: dictionary
lesson: 13823
title: Words from long ago
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: The Israelites were a people of long ago, whose story is told in the Bible. Israelites is a plural word, so it has an s on the end. One person of that people is an Israelite.
explain: Look at the words around it for clues. «Moses led the Israelites out of Egypt.» The people were led out of a place, and the story tells you they were a people with a history of their own, not a name for a country today.
explain: Be careful with a similar word. Israelis are the citizens of the modern state of Israel today. Israelites are the people of ancient times. Check the sentence: is it talking about long ago, or about today?
fact: Israelites is a plural noun, and the singular is Israelite.
fact: The Israelites were the people of ancient Israel, the descendants of Jacob (also called Israel) and his twelve sons.
fact: «The Israelites wandered in the desert for forty years.»
fact: Israelis are the citizens of the modern state of Israel today; the two words are not the same.
fact: Israelites starts with a capital letter because it is the name of a people.
exercise: «Moses led the Israelites out of Egypt.» Who was led out of Egypt? | The Egyptians | The twelve kings of Rome | The desert animals | *The Israelites
exercise: What is the singular of Israelites? | Israel | *Israelite | Israeli | Israelitess
exercise: «The Israelites wandered in the desert for forty years.» How long did they wander? | Four years | *Forty years | Four hundred years | Forty days
test: «The Israelites were slaves in Egypt.» Where were the Israelites slaves? | In Scotland | *In Egypt | In Rome | In ancient Greece
test: Today's citizens of the state of Israel are called what? | Jacobs | Israelites | Egyptians | *Israelis
exam: Which word is the correct singular for «the Israelites»? | *Israelite | Israelites | Israel | Israeli
